  "boundary": "Shared manifest across separate rewrap, payload and search rotations; source-only cancellation, exact PostgreSQL frames/terms/uniqueness and latest-value removal. Actual AppRole-authenticated native OpenBao version 1 to 2 rewrap. Independent retained PostgreSQL backup recovery with explicit restored-target rotation planning.",
  "failures_retained": [
    "Two initial refusal assertions expected a generic pin code; the existing executors correctly returned purpose-specific rotation pin mismatch codes. Expectations corrected.",
    "The second installed OpenBao run failed a 15s Doctor subprocess watchdog and a 5s warm lease after a container stop with a 10s grace period. No fallback or unauthenticated value was returned.",
    "The process watchdog now accommodates two bounded 10s RPCs plus startup. The outage test uses an explicit 30s lease, waits for actual expiry, and still requires held and fresh access to refuse.",
    "The first explicit shared-configuration restore selection omitted the prerequisite backup-restore test and failed on the absent schema. The profile now selects both restore/authentication and the configuration journey, and requires two passing restore calls.",
    "One later source-only invalid-context Doctor subprocess timed out after 45s despite requiring no provider I/O. Its cause remains UNKNOWN; the subsequent isolated source run is retained separately, without a product retry or timeout change.",
    "The first installed run predates the separate shared-configuration restore profile and native key-version change; its narrower boundary is retained."
  ],
  "limits": [
